WEBVTT

00:00:01.880 --> 00:00:05.880
Welcome to the Microsoft for Education Daily, Thursday edition.

00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:10.270
Here are the last 24 hours at Microsoft, in 3 minutes.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:18.390
Make it yours. Microsoft Classroom puts assignments,

00:00:18.390 --> 00:00:22.170
grades and more in one place, from primary to university.

00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:27.460
Admins can sign up today; the preview is planned for early 2027.

00:00:31.880 --> 00:00:34.660
Students will get one home for what's due,

00:00:34.660 --> 00:00:38.190
what's overdue and new feedback, across every class.

00:00:39.380 --> 00:00:41.940
Teachers will see what needs grading, and Teach,

00:00:41.940 --> 00:00:44.870
Microsoft's AI planning space, will be built right in.

00:00:46.880 --> 00:00:53.400
It'll be included with A2, A3, A5 and A7 at no extra cost, and Teams stays.

00:00:53.910 --> 00:00:59.080
Teaching research? Add -ai to any Bing search to skip the AI answers.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:01.890
Coding class in Visual Studio?

00:01:01.890 --> 00:01:05.860
You can now bring your own AI model, even one running locally.

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:10.410
Hook up Foundry, OpenAI, Anthropic,

00:01:10.410 --> 00:01:14.730
Ollama or LM Studio, with no GitHub sign-in needed.

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:16.790
Student projects on GitHub?

00:01:16.790 --> 00:01:22.020
Personal accounts now get issue types and fields, like bug, task and priority.

00:01:22.500 --> 00:01:26.910
Teams is due to let school IT choose who can record and transcribe meetings,

00:01:26.910 --> 00:01:27.780
from December.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:30.720
In the lab,

00:01:30.720 --> 00:01:36.240
Microsoft researchers edited under 10 neurons to hide a trigger inside an AI model.

00:01:37.500 --> 00:01:39.390
The good news? It can be caught,

00:01:39.390 --> 00:01:42.990
so get models from their original publisher, and check them.

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:48.810
The fine print? November's updates fix over 1,000 flaws,

00:01:48.810 --> 00:01:52.070
including an Outlook bug attackers already use.

00:01:52.500 --> 00:01:58.350
And Windows 11 23H2 Education just got its final update, so plan the upgrade.

00:02:01.880 --> 00:02:03.890
After hours, for Halo's 25th,

00:02:03.890 --> 00:02:08.460
Flight Simulator lets you fly its Pelican free until November 17.

00:02:09.380 --> 00:02:11.190
On the ROG Xbox Ally X,

00:02:11.190 --> 00:02:16.070
Microsoft's AI upscaling now works handheld, even on battery.

00:02:16.880 --> 00:02:21.740
And Luma Island hits Xbox December 2, with a peaceful Cozy Mode.

00:02:22.500 --> 00:02:26.630
Your class, your model, your search, your game: make it yours.

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:32.820
Every day, the changelog gets a little longer.

00:02:33.750 --> 00:02:37.340
Today's board: shipped. Tomorrow's: already building.

00:02:37.500 --> 00:02:40.970
That's one day of updates. Imagine a whole year.

00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:47.950
That's the Microsoft for Education Daily for today.

00:02:48.750 --> 00:02:50.120
Same time tomorrow?
